<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>The Use of Large Language Models (LLMs)</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We strictly adhere to the ICLR Code of Ethics and only utilize the Large Language Model to polish the paper for grammar and expression checks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Limitation and Future Works</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our study focuses on small (1.5B) and medium (7B) models due to limited computational resources. Scaling the method to larger models is a promising direction for future work. Our approach primarily targets full-parameter SFT; when applying parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT), the freezing strategy may need to be adjusted to prevent catastrophic forgetting between SFT and RL. As stronger SFT and RL algorithms continue to emerge, we release this plug-and-play framework to encourage the community to explore improved post-training reasoning with advanced algorithm combinations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Theoretical Insights and Proof</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide theoretical insights trying to explain why SFT exhibits greater redundancy in parameter updates than RL. The following discussion and proofs rest on simplifying assumptions intended to interpret our empirical findings, instead of providing a rigorous theoretical guarantee. Because large language models involve extremely high-dimensional parameters and massive training data, fully rigorous modeling is challenging.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Redundancy Ratio Definition</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ C.1 Redundancy Ratio Definition ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> to describe the <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">decision–redundancy ratio</span> (DR) as a way to quantify how wasteful a parameter update is. For a given input and target token, we look at the strongest non-target competitor under the current parameters and measure the logit margin between the target and that competitor. Assuming the margin changes approximately linearly with small parameter moves and the same competitor remains active, there exists a unique, shortest move in parameter space that achieves any desired margin increase; this move points along the margin’s gradient. DR is then defined as the size of the actual parameter change divided by the size of the shortest move. A larger DR means the training trajectory moved farther than necessary to achieve the same decision margin, indicating more redundant updating.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a context <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and target token <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{1,\dots,V\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{1,\dots,V\}</annotation></semantics></math> with vocabulary size <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be model parameters and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> a reference point (e.g., pre-update).
For logits <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>V</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and probabilities <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}=\mathrm{softmax}(z_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the active competitor at <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\star}=\arg\max_{k\neq y}z_{\theta_{0},k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\star}=\arg\max_{k\neq y}z_{\theta_{0},k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The (logit) decision margin is
<math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta)=z_{\theta,y}(x)-z_{\theta,k^{\star}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta)=z_{\theta,y}(x)-z_{\theta,k^{\star}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{0}=m(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{0}=m(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, and
its parameter gradient is <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\nabla_{\theta}m(\theta_{0})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\nabla_{\theta}m(\theta_{0})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume (A1) local linearity <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\theta_{0}+\Delta)\approx m_{0}+g^{\top}\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\theta_{0}+\Delta)\approx m_{0}+g^{\top}\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for
small <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and (A2) competitor stability (the same <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> remains active locally).
Then for any desired margin <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the minimal parameter displacement <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> that achieves margin <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}=\arg\min_{\Delta}\{\|\Delta\|_{2}:\ g^{\top}\Delta\geq\varepsilon-m_{0}\}=\frac{\varepsilon-m_{0}}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\,g,\qquad\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}=\frac{\varepsilon-m_{0}}{\|g\|_{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}=\arg\min_{\Delta}\{\|\Delta\|_{2}:\ g^{\top}\Delta\geq\varepsilon-m_{0}\}=\frac{\varepsilon-m_{0}}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\,g,\qquad\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}=\frac{\varepsilon-m_{0}}{\|g\|_{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and for any training trajectory with net update <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta=\theta_{T}-\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta=\theta_{T}-\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have decision–redundancy ratio</span></p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\coloneqq\varepsilon-m_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\coloneqq\varepsilon-m_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under (A1) local linearity and (A2) competitor stability, achieving the (linearized) target margin <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to requiring</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\top}\Delta\;\geq\;\beta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\top}\Delta\;\geq\;\beta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=\nabla_{\theta}m(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=\nabla_{\theta}m(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the minimal-displacement problem is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}=\min_{\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\ \|\Delta\|_{2}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad g^{\top}\Delta\geq\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}=\min_{\Delta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\ \|\Delta\|_{2}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad g^{\top}\Delta\geq\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible and optimal (the target margin is already met), and the result is trivial. In the remainder, assume <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any feasible <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>, by Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\;\leq\;g^{\top}\Delta\;\leq\;\|g\|_{2}\,\|\Delta\|_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\Delta\|_{2}\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\;\leq\;g^{\top}\Delta\;\leq\;\|g\|_{2}\,\|\Delta\|_{2}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\|\Delta\|_{2}\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Equality holds if and only if <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is colinear and aligned with <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\alpha g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\alpha g</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\Delta^{\star}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\,g,\qquad\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>β</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\quad\Rightarrow\quad\Delta^{\star}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}^{2}}\,g,\qquad\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\|g\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the lower bound and is the unique minimizer (any deviation from the <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> direction increases the norm for fixed inner product <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\top}\Delta=\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\top}\Delta=\beta</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider any training trajectory with net update <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\theta=\theta_{T}-\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\theta=\theta_{T}-\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> that attains the target margin in the linearized model, so <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\top}\Delta\theta\geq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\top}\Delta\theta\geq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. By optimality of <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\geq\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\geq\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}\;\equiv\;\frac{\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}\;=\;\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≡</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}\;\equiv\;\frac{\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}\;=\;\|\Delta\theta\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">(When <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\star}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\star}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and the margin is already satisfied.)
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the decision–redundancy ratio (DR) defined in the previous section, we now analyze the properties of SFT and RL based on their gradient. We first borrow the policy gradient form of SFT from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, and then compare their decision–redundancy ratios.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SFT Gradient.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x,y^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x,y^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a corpus of annotated demonstrations, where <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reference response for query <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
SFT minimizes the cross-entropy loss:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and its gradient is:</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RL Gradient.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> denote a rollout response sampled from the policy model <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> for query <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a reward function <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the policy objective is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[r(x,y)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[r(x,y)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and its policy gradient is</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\;r(x,y)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\;r(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rewriting SFT Gradient as Policy Gradient.</span>
Here we directly quote the conclusion from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025)</a></cite> to rewrite SFT gradient to policy gradient. The SFT gradient in Equation <a href="#A3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ SFT Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> taken under the fixed demonstration distribution is convert it to an on-policy expectation by inserting an importance weight that compares the expert (Dirac Delta) distribution with the model distribution:</p>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x}}\;\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}[y=y^{*}]}{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}\;\big(-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\big)\right]}_{\text{resample + reweight}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>resample + reweight</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{*})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[-\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y^{*}\mid x)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x}}\;\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\left[\frac{\mathbb{I}[y=y^{*}]}{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)}\;\big(-\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\big)\right]}_{\text{resample + reweight}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Define the auxiliary variables</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w(y\mid x)=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)},\qquad r(x,y)=\mathbb{I}[y=y^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(y\mid x)=\frac{1}{\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)},\qquad r(x,y)=\mathbb{I}[y=y^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Reorganize Equation <a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and rewrite it using the above auxiliary variables; we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\Big[w(y\mid x)\;\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\;r(x,y)\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.447em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}_{x},\;y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)}\!\Big[w(y\mid x)\;\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\;r(x,y)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This form of the SFT gradient now closely aligns with the policy gradient in Equation <a href="#A3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>:
Conventional SFT can be viewed as an on-policy gradient where the reward is an indicator of matching the expert response, modulated by an importance weight <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we will utilize obtained conclusions to analyze DR of SFT and RL.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the reward function as <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> for the policy model <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a input context <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, policy model output token <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> according to <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and target token <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]\;\geq\;r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]\;\geq\;r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, SFT (policy model expression) and RL predict <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that both attain the same target margin <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\geq\;\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{RL}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>RL</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\geq\;\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{RL}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Equation <a href="#A3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Lemma 1. ‣ C.1 Redundancy Ratio Definition ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ C.1 Redundancy Ratio Definition ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have the following DR for SFT and RL:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta^{SFT}\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta^{SFT}\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}=\|\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta^{SFT}\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta^{SFT}\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}=\|\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}(\theta)\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta^{RL}\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta^{RL}\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}=\|\eta\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}\equiv\frac{\|\Delta\theta^{RL}\|_{2}}{\|\Delta^{\star}\|_{2}}=\|\Delta\theta^{RL}\|_{2}\cdot\frac{\|g\|_{2}}{\varepsilon-m_{0}}=\|\eta\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then we utilize the sentence level policy gradient expressions in Equation <a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and Equation <a href="#A3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Here we make slight change from the sentence level expression to token level expression here to simplify the illustration and have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}}{\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}}=\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}\|_{2}}{\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|_{2}}=\frac{\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]}{r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)}\;\geq\;1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}}{\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}}=\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}\|_{2}}{\|\nabla_{\theta}J(\theta)\|_{2}}=\frac{\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]}{r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)}\;\geq\;1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">So we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\geq\;\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{RL}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>RL</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\geq\;\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{\mathrm{RL}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> provides the condition when <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{SFT}</annotation></semantics></math> will larger then <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>DR</mi><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DR}_{x}^{RL}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since when SFT updates, the gradient in Equation <a href="#A3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ RL Gradient. ‣ C.2 Redundancy Analysis of SFT and RL ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Insights and Proof ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> can’t be zero, therefore <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>. And for hard reasoning case, the policy probability <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> while reward function <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is usually bounded (PPO/GRPO), therefore <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p10.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]\;\geq\;r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[y_{t}=y^{*}_{t}]\;\geq\;r\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and SFT has more updating redundancy compared to RL.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MIFO</span>: MItigating FOrgetting between SFT and RL</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          Policy <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, old policy <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, reward <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, entropy ratio <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, decay <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, Buffer size <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, SFT data D.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          Initialize <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Buffer</mtext><mtext>FT</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}^{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}^{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>, Define <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SFT}\to\text{RL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>SFT</mtext><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>RL</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SFT}\to\text{RL}</annotation></semantics></math> iteration <math id="alg1.l2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="alg1.l2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Interval}^{RL\to SFT}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext>Interval</mtext><mi>i</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Interval}^{RL\to SFT}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Interval}^{RL\to SFT}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mtext>Interval</mtext><mi>i</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Interval}^{RL\to SFT}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> interval iteration <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Record <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\text{j}}_{RL,start,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>j</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\text{j}}_{RL,start,i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each question <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> rollout, compute <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(o_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(o_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and advantages <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Update <math id="alg1.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> via GRPO

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{acc}(q)&lt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{acc}(q)&lt;a</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{extract}(D(q))=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>extract</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{extract}(D(q))=a</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
               Add <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,D(q))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,D(q))</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Buffer</mtext><mtext>FT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Record <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{\text{j}}_{RL,end,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mtext>j</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{\text{j}}_{RL,end,i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{RL},i}^{j}\leftarrow\left\|\theta_{\mathrm{RL,end},i}^{j}-\theta_{\mathrm{RL,start},i}^{j}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>RL</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>RL</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>end</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>RL</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>start</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{RL},i}^{j}\leftarrow\left\|\theta_{\mathrm{RL,end},i}^{j}-\theta_{\mathrm{RL,start},i}^{j}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{C}}_{i}\;=\;\alpha\,\bm{C}_{i-1}\;+\;(1-\alpha)\,\Delta\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{RL},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑪</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>RL</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{C}}_{i}\;=\;\alpha\,\bm{C}_{i-1}\;+\;(1-\alpha)\,\Delta\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{RL},i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Obtain the mask <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}=\mathbf{1}[\,j\in\mathcal{I}_{i}\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}=\mathbf{1}[\,j\in\mathcal{I}_{i}\,]</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="alg1.l13.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}=\mathbf{1}[\,j\in\mathcal{I}_{i}\,],\mathbf{C}_{i}\;=\;\mathbf{M}_{i}\odot\tilde{\mathbf{C}}_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐂</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i}^{j}=\mathbf{1}[\,j\in\mathcal{I}_{i}\,],\mathbf{C}_{i}\;=\;\mathbf{M}_{i}\odot\tilde{\mathbf{C}}_{i},</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            Freeze Selected parameters <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\bm{\theta}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\leftarrow\;(\mathbf{1}-\mathbf{M}_{i})\odot\nabla_{\bm{\theta}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SFT</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\bm{\theta}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}\;\leftarrow\;(\mathbf{1}-\mathbf{M}_{i})\odot\nabla_{\bm{\theta}_{i}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SFT}}.</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
            SFT only calculate loss for tokens with <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}\geq\tau_{\rho}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}\geq\tau_{\rho}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Buffer</mtext><mtext>FT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Buffer}_{\text{FT}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and unfreeze.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Method Implementation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement RL and SFT following widely used settings. For RL, we remove the KL penalty, length normalization, and standard-error normalization, as in Dr.GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025c</a>)</cite> and LUFFY <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. GRPO hyperparameters are: rollout batch size <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math>, number of rollouts per query <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>, update batch size <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, rollout temperature <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, and entropy coefficient <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.
For SFT, the training batch size is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> and the learning rate is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>. For MIFO, the rollout-accuracy threshold for buffering is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\tfrac{1}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\tfrac{1}{8}</annotation></semantics></math>, the high-entropy token ratio is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, the TopK freezing fraction is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and the decay coefficient is <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. Pseudocode of MIFO is provided in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix D Implementation Details ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cui et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025c</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we train on Qwen2.5-Math (1.5B and 7B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. As in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we increase the RoPE base from <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> and extend the context window to <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16{,}384" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16,384</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16{,}384</annotation></semantics></math> tokens to encourage exploration. Models are trained for three epochs on <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 8</annotation></semantics></math> A100 GPUs using the VERL framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. The reward is binary:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if the answer is correct},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if the answer is correct</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if the answer is correct},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Except for Oat-Zero and OpenReasoner-7B, we independently evaluate publicly released baseline checkpoints to reproduce and verify prior results. The remaining baseline scores are taken from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which adopts the same evaluation protocol as MIFO. All evaluations are conducted with vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, using a temperature of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and a maximum sequence length of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8{,}192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8,192</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8{,}192</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. Additional dataset statistics are provided in Table <a href="#A4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Evaluation ‣ Appendix D Implementation Details ‣ Mitigating Forgetting Between Supervised and Reinforcement Learning Yields Stronger Reasoners" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>The statistics of evaluation datasets</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Dataset</th>
<th id="A4.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">#Test</th>
<th id="A4.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Task Type</th>
<th id="A4.T4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Domain</th>
<th id="A4.T4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">#k</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">AIME24</td>
<td id="A4.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">30</td>
<td id="A4.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Math competition</td>
